{"continue":{"clcontinue":"92460408|Books_uploaded_by_F\u00e6/reviewed","continue":"||imageinfo"},"query":{"pages":{"92460408":{"pageid":92460408,"ns":6,"title":"File:A historical perspective of aircrew systems effects on aircraft design (IA historicalperspe00baue).pdf","index":2,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":5939524,"width":816,"height":1118,"pagecount":116,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/A_historical_perspective_of_aircrew_systems_effects_on_aircraft_design_%28IA_historicalperspe00baue%29.pdf/page1-500px-A_historical_perspective_of_aircrew_systems_effects_on_aircraft_design_%28IA_historicalperspe00baue%29.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":960,"thumbheight":1315,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/A_historical_perspective_of_aircrew_systems_effects_on_aircraft_design_%28IA_historicalperspe00baue%29.pdf/page1-500px-A_historical_perspective_of_aircrew_systems_effects_on_aircraft_design_%28IA_historicalperspe00baue%29.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":960,"height":1315},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/93/A_historical_perspective_of_aircrew_systems_effects_on_aircraft_design_%28IA_historicalperspe00baue%29.pdf?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_historical_perspective_of_aircrew_systems_effects_on_aircraft_design_(IA_historicalperspe00baue).pdf","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=92460408","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2020-07-21 19:21:21","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"<div class=\"fn\">\nA historical perspective of aircrew systems effects on aircraft design</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"PD US Government|Scans from the Internet Archive/unverified|CC-PD-Mark|Scans from the Internet Archive|Books uploaded by F\u00e6/reviewed|Books without Wikidata item|Documents from the US Naval Postgraduate School Library/reviewed|Books from the United States PDF files|1996 books about aviation|Master's theses of the Naval Postgraduate School","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Artist":{"value":"<div class=\"fn value\">\nBauer, David O.</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<div class=\"description\">\n<dl><dd>Thesis advisor(s): Conrad F. Newberry</dd>\n<dd>\"September 1996.\"</dd>\n<dd>Thesis (M.S. in Aeronautical Engineering) Naval Postgraduate School, September 1996</dd>\n<dd>Includes bibliographical references (p. 99-100)</dd>\n<dd>The design of the aircrew workstation often has not been an orderly part of the overall aircraft design process but rather of much lower priority than the integration of the airframe and powerplant. However, the true test of the aircraft is how well the aircrew can use the aircraft for mission performance. NAVAIR has been seeking the establishment of an Aircrew Centered System Design discipline, to be addressed as an integral part of the global aircraft system design process. A baseline, historical understanding of how the aircrew have been integrated into the aircraft and mission is needed. An analysis was conducted of several significant airplanes from the Wright Flyer to the present, seeking those design factors which affected how well the aircrew were able to perform the design mission. The physical and attentional resources of the aircrew must be understood and accommodated by those designing the cockpit and other workstations. Aircrew members who are knowledgeable of, and experienced in the intended mission must be involved in the design process from the very earliest phases of concept definition</dd>\n<dd>Mode of access: World Wide Web</dd>\n<dd>System requirements: Adobe Acrobat Reader</dd>\n<dd>US Navy (USN) author</dd>\n<dd>dk/dk cc:9116 07/23/97</dd></dl>\n<br>Subjects:</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<dl><dd><a href=\"//archive.org/details/historicalperspe00baue\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"iarchive:historicalperspe00baue\"><bdi class=\"description en\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">Internet Archive identifier</bdi>: historicalperspe00baue</a></dd>\n<dd><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://archive.org/download/historicalperspe00baue/historicalperspe00baue.pdf\">https://archive.org/download/historicalperspe00baue/historicalperspe00baue.pdf</a></dd></dl>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}},"mime":"application/pdf"}],"categories":[{"ns":14,"title":"Category:1996 books about aviation"},{"ns":14,"title":"Category:Books from the United States PDF files"}]},"153103350":{"pageid":153103350,"ns":6,"title":"File:Advances in hydrologic engineering - USACE-p16021coll8-2930.pdf","index":1,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":1961120,"width":1275,"height":1650,"pagecount":13,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Advances_in_hydrologic_engineering_-_USACE-p16021coll8-2930.pdf/page1-960px-Advances_in_hydrologic_engineering_-_USACE-p16021coll8-2930.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":960,"thumbheight":1242,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikime